{# narrative_engine/plot_prepare — what must be done before a planned step.
   Asked by PlotPlanning::Plan once the goal is planned, again after each
   preparation is added, until the answer is ready or the plan is full.
   Each option is a whole step, already about the right people, and says
   which planned step it comes just before. The answer is p1 onward, or
   ready.
   Receives: mastermind { name, standing }, bio, ambition, scheme,
     history [string] (steps already taken, when re-planning), plan
     [string] (the steps planned so far, numbered, the last being the one
     that accomplishes the scheme), options [{ key, line }].
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state who ]
{{ mastermind.name }}{% if length(mastermind.standing) > 0 %}, {{ mastermind.standing }}{% endif %}.
{{ bio.summary }}
[ end state ]

[ state aims ]
The scheme: {{ scheme }}
[ end state ]

{% if length(history) > 0 %}[ state history ]
What has already happened:
{% for s in history %}{{ s }}
{% endfor %}[ end state ]

{% endif %}[ state plan ]
The steps planned so far, in order; the last one accomplishes the scheme:
{% for s in plan %}{{ s }}
{% endfor %}[ end state ]

[ question prepare choice ]
Is there something `who` should have done first, to make a step in `plan` more likely to work? Each choice is done just before the step it names. Choose ready if the plan in `plan` can be carried out as it stands.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.line }}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
